Prior work this is built on
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The techniques implemented here were not all originated by this project:

  * The use of NVIDIA's PRI decode traps as a privilege-escalation primitive
    (a trap armed with ACTION.SET_PRIV_LEVEL and DATA1 = 0xC0000000 stamping a
    matching host write to level 3) was discovered by BlackSun on the
    NVIDIA CMP 170HX. This project ports that mechanism to Volta.

  * The SPI write procedure (driving SPI_CTRL / SPI_DATA_ARRAY directly to
    issue JEDEC frames, bypassing the vendor flash utility) is zorg33's work,
    also from the CMP 170HX.

  * The firmware defect the privilege escalation relies on is NVIDIA's own, as
    is the identifier it was later given in their firmware,
    NV_PREOS_ERR_INFOROM_BUFFER_OVERFLOW.

